---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../site';

const credits = [
  { name: 'pdf-lib', license: 'MIT', url: 'https://github.com/Hopding/pdf-lib' },
  { name: 'PDF.js', license: 'Apache-2.0', url: 'https://github.com/mozilla/pdf.js' },
  { name: 'Ghostscript', license: 'AGPL-3.0', url: 'https://www.ghostscript.com/' },
  { name: 'ghostpdl-wasm', license: 'AGPL-3.0', url: 'https://github.com/okathira/ghostpdl-wasm' },
  { name: 'fflate', license: 'MIT', url: 'https://github.com/101arrowz/fflate' },
  { name: 'dnd kit', license: 'MIT', url: 'https://github.com/clauderic/dnd-kit' },
];
---

<Base
  title={`How ${site.name} keeps your files private`}
  description={`${site.name} processes PDFs entirely in your browser. Here's how it works and how to verify that nothing is uploaded.`}
>
  <article class="container prose">
    <h1>How {site.name} works</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      {site.name} is a set of PDF tools that run entirely in your browser. Your files are never uploaded, stored, or
      seen by anyone.
    </p>

    <h2>What happens to your file</h2>
    <p>
      When you choose a PDF, your browser reads it from your disk into memory. The tool processes it right there,
      using code that was downloaded with the page, and hands the result back to you as a download. When you close
      the tab, it's gone.
    </p>

    <h2>How to check for yourself</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Go offline.</strong> Load a tool page, turn off your wifi, then use the tool. It keeps working because
        it never needed a server.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Watch the network.</strong> Open your browser's developer tools, go to the Network tab, and process
        a file. You'll see no request carrying your PDF.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Read the security policy.</strong> Every page sends a Content-Security-Policy that only allows
        connections back to this site, plus cookieless visit counting. Your browser enforces it even if the code
        tried to send your file elsewhere.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Analytics</h2>
    <p>
      We count page visits with Cloudflare Web Analytics, which uses no cookies and doesn't track you across sites.
      It never sees your files.
    </p>

    <h2>Open source</h2>
    <p>
      {site.name} is free software under the GNU AGPL-3.0 license. The full source code is at
      <a href={site.sourceUrl} rel="noopener">{site.sourceUrl.replace('https://', '')}</a>.
    </p>
    <p>It is built on these open-source projects:</p>
    <ul>
      {
        credits.map((credit) => (
          <li>
            <a href={credit.url} rel="noopener">
              {credit.name}
            </a>{' '}
            ({credit.license})
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ul>

    <p>Made by <a href={site.studioUrl} rel="noopener">{site.studio}</a>.</p>
  </article>
</Base>
